  "description": "A rear single-storey extension of 6m depth, with a flat roof, sloping down to 2.70m towards the north boundary.\nThe extension steps back from the north boundary by 600mm to reduce overshadowing of the neighbours' premises.\nThe extension's roof slopes down to 2.70m towards the north boundary to maintain daylight and sunlight to the neighbour's garden.\n\n15 Cedar Grove is the property to the north of the applicant plot. The spaces on the ground floor facing the garden are a toilet, which is next to the shared boundary, a hallway leading to the garden and a kitchen with its window next to the boundary to No 17.\n\nThe proposed extension will not affect the daylight and sunlight exposure of the kitchen and hallway windows and door.\nThe proposal is sympathetic to the surroundings and modest in size and proportion.\n\nThe proposed materials will match the existing materials to ensure a coherent appearance with the existing buildings.\n",
